        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(signal): add setup wizard",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSignal setup needed a guided path that proves a usable receive transport before users rely on the channel, without OpenClaw creating or managing a Signal Docker container. Existing setup and status paths could also leave stale native/container transport fields ambiguous, miss account-specific API-mode behavior, or report a Signal daemon as generically working when the configured account was missing or receive was unavailable.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Signal plugin now owns a setup wizard path for two supported transports: local `signal-cli` and an existing Signal server managed by the operator. The same change tightens native/container/auto probing so setup and status can distinguish transport reachability from account/receive readiness, and it lets multi-account Signal configs use `channels.signal.apiMode` as a channel default with per-account overrides.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can run Signal setup, choose local `signal-cli` or an existing server URL, and have setup save config only after the selected transport is reachable for the intended account. Operators get clearer `openclaw channels status --probe` and health output for ready, account-missing, receive-unavailable, and unreachable Signal states. Existing/manual `bbernhard/signal-cli-rest-api` deployments remain supported through `apiMode: \"container\"`; OpenClaw no longer offers an OpenClaw-managed Signal Docker setup path.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBehavioral proof:\n\n- Existing-server setup prompts for a Signal account, probes the server with that account, and saves `httpUrl`, `autoStart: false`, and `apiMode: \"auto\"` after the probe succeeds.\n- Native setup clears stale external/container endpoint fields for the intended account while preserving existing custom native endpoints and channel-level `channels.signal.apiMode` defaults.\n- Container receive readiness is checked through `/v1/receive/{account}` when receive capability is required, and container account validation uses bounded `/v1/accounts` reads.\n- Signal send, reaction, monitor, attachment, and probe paths now resolve account-specific `apiMode` before falling back to the channel default.\n- `openclaw channels status --probe` and health formatting expose Signal readiness states instead of reducing account-missing/receive-unavailable cases to a generic “works” signal.\n- Screenshots are omitted because this PR changes terminal/setup wizard, gateway status, config, docs, and tests rather than browser UI; command output is the reviewer-checkable proof.\n\nAutomated checks on head `dd7d8eee32e9cc23f6a39f8a5fff87a8dc8c8ac5`:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/setup-entry.test.ts extensions/signal/src/core.test.ts extensions/signal/src/setup-core.test.ts extensions/signal/src/client-adapter.test.ts extensions/signal/src/client-container.test.ts extensions/signal/src/client.test.ts extensions/signal/src/config-schema.test.ts extensions/signal/src/install-signal-cli.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor.tool-result.pairs-uuid-only-senders-uuid-allowlist-entry.test.ts extensions/signal/src/send-reactions.test.ts extensions/signal/src/send.test.ts src/commands/channels.surfaces-signal-runtime-errors-channels-status-output.test.ts src/commands/health.test.ts src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.test.ts` passed: 14 files across 3 Vitest shards, 394 tests.\n- `corepack pnpm config:docs:check` passed.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-bundled-channel-config-metadata.ts --check` passed.\n- `corepack pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check` passed.\n- `corepack pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/signal/src/setup-core.ts extensions/signal/src/setup-core.test.ts extensions/signal/src/core.test.ts extensions/signal/src/send-reactions.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor.tool-result.pairs-uuid-only-senders-uuid-allowlist-entry.test.ts` passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\nReview proof:\n\n- Native review phase reached two clean passes on the final production target before the final test-only coverage additions.\n- Final independent review, test-audit, and TypeScript/API-contract review on head `dd7d8eee32e9cc23f6a39f8a5fff87a8dc8c8ac5` found no actionable issues after the account-scoped `apiMode` coverage fixes.\n\nKnown proof limits:\n\n- No manual Signal messages were sent.\n- No real `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` config was touched.\n",
        "branch": "jesse/signal-setup-wizard",
